Brief outline of activity:

【1】Students are given the requirement and details about building a system to calculate the actual price of movie tickets based on user’s age, 
height and disable status. 

【2】Students are encouraged to discuss with their neighbor and write the code plan together. 
They are asked to come up with different solutions as many as possible. 

【3】After finishing the code, professors will show how to write this code. Students are encouraged to show their different solutions.

【4】Students are given a bunch of practice that involve different use of == and =. “or” and “and”. 
They are required to justify which one is incorrect and debug it. 

【5】Students are given a special example which can satisfy at least 2 conditions. 
They are required to explain the order of conditions, and whether it matters deciding the prices.





Main Exercise — Movie Ticket Pricing

Write a program that calculates movie ticket prices based on the following rules:

Age 6 or younger: free ticket.

Height 1.2 meters or below: free ticket.

Eligible for a disability discount: 50% off.

Otherwise: regular price.

Ask for entering the original price of movie tickets first. If multiple discounts apply, use the lowest applicable ticket price.


